do we finally know where the last two  remaining road ponoglyphs are that the  striats still need to find so they can  finally reach love tape well at the very  least we have just gotten a few major  clues and a bunch of new information  dropped on our heads there are three  likely locations for it albath an island  called vida and beehive island  blackbeard's base of operation and as i  will explain to you i personally believe  that elbaf and shanks are the most  likely candidates here now you might be  like manu where is this information  coming from there is no one piece  chapter this week well wrong kind of  even though the one piece manga is on a  four week break at the moment each year  order the author of one piece has  decided to release a series of four mini  booklets as a small gift to readers in  every release of shonen jump in the  meantime instead this little series is  titled the road to love tale and  documents or senses preparation for the  final saga of one piece these booklets  contain a lot of character sketches and  recaps of things we already know however  there are also some very chunky nuggets  of fresh information and reveals to be  found there as well and so the very  first volume that's out now is focused  very heavily on roger and how he became  pirate king dedicating a whole page to  the mysterious poneglyphs and by far the  biggest thing in all of this i think is  that oda sensei discusses the locations  of the four road pony cliffs here we  have of course already the two that the  straw hats have in their possession the  one from zou and one from big mom that  broke heroically made a successful  rubbing off similar to how roger got his  hands on it actually the third road  poneglyph roger found in wano itself and  the last one was located in fishman  island where it stood right next to  joyboy's apology ladder to the mermaid  princess now funnily enough we didn't  actually know for a fact whether the  third road poneglyph was still in one or  not all we've seen so far are two of the  30 plus real pony glyphs that detail the  history of the void century however this  booklet now tells us for sure that  kaido's rule over a closed border wano  has kept anyone else from getting their  hands on his road poneglyph which is a  huge deal in a number of ways because i  think it basically the first time we  officially get confirmed that it's still  waiting right here in wano for the straw  hats to be found and as we all know that  basically means that the straw hats very  very soon will get their hands on it it  also means we still have another story  threat that needs to happen in wano  which makes me happy because i really  didn't want to leave the country as  quickly as the last few chapters made it  originally seen however it also means  that other people probably know that the  poneglyph is here and might now come for  the very same road podoglyph i'm  thinking of course blackbeard and for  some reason now also buggy luffy's two  main rivals to becoming pirate king  because blackbeard surely would have  been fully aware of kaido sitting on top  of that particular red stone it might  also be the reason or at least one of  the reasons why momo decided to leave  wanos borders closed for now at least  until luffy reaches love tale telling  sunisha basically well thanks for  dropping by but you know could you come  back at a more convenient time please  and so the fact that a road poneglyph is  located in wano also adds a lot more  weight to the reveal that odin's father  and momonosuke's grandfather kozuki  sukiyaki former shogun of wano and heir  to the kazuki clan is still alive i  don't know how but i somehow totally  overlooked that in the last chapter but  he was obviously the one who taught odin  how to read and write the language of  the ancient kingdom in other words oda  just snuck another character back into  the story that can potentially lead the  way to the final islands this is huge  sukiyaki might be the lottery ticket  someone like blackbeard has been waiting  for to make his way to love tale as well  should he not be able to get his hands  on robin because him and robin are  pretty much the only two confirmed  people alive who can't read this  language and decipher the pony glyphs  and should blackbeard make his way to  wano to get it and find out who sukiyaki  really is  that would be a true advantage falling  into his hands but i mean as if this  wasn't enough already oda sensei also  decided to tease us with the location of  the last remaining lost road poneglyph  that used to be on fishman islands and  he gives us three possible locations  here elbaf beehive island itself and  vida now you might be asking what a  usopp is a vita well it's actually an  island that was named in the story  before by nami very early on in the  story as she's reading nolan's journal  in other words vida is an island that  was visited by noland 400 years ago and  was described as a very lively and happy  place well since then we found out that  this small town expanded into a  full-blown country but it no longer is  the happy place you can easily live and  smile at instead it was ruled by a  tyrannical government probably  associated with the world nobles and so  after the breakout of a major rebellion  two years ago it was finally freed by  the revolutionary army now sensei of  course does mention here as well that  there are other possibilities for the  location as he should if we're being  honest but he still chose to focus on  these three specifically and i think it  makes sense because all three of these  islands seem to have ties to powerful  people who might have gotten their hands  on the last rode pony glyph veena is  connected to the revolutionaries and  dragon who clearly know quite a lot  about the true history which was why  robin in particular got sent to them by  kuma in the first place so maybe vita is  now the island that the revolutionaries  have moved their scent of operation to  after they got raided by blackbeard's  crew on their previous base and who  knows maybe blackbeard came for them  exactly because he knew that they had a  road poneglyph which of course already  brings us to beehive island it used to  be the base for rox diesel back who by  the way also has a whole page dedicated  to him in this booklet that details his  connections to blackbeard who also named  his ship the zebek now this place is  blackbeard's home and since blackbit is  also aiming to become pirate king it  would really not be too far-fetched to  think that he already has gotten his  hands on a pony glyph there as well  though i would say it's not quite as  likely as the last one because lastly  there is elbaf not only has elba been  hinted at over and over and over again  to be the next island the straw heads  will travel to after wano as i've  discussed in previous videos i mean you  have usop's relationship to the giants  big mom's relationship to the giants the  introduction of loki and so on but it  also seems like elbaf has very strong  ties to another yonko shanks as i've  explained in his character analysis  shanks has a very strong viking theme  going on there's of course a ship that  has the exact same style as dory and  braggi's but shanks is also inspired by  the nordic god tier who has also lost an  arm to a beast and enough of other  parallels as well we also know that the  yonko including shanks holds territory  in the new world again something that is  discussed in detail in the road to love  tale here territorial dispute in the new  world between the yonko and ko and so i  have always been a very strong supporter  of the idea  that elbaf is part of shanks's territory  his home turf in the new world if you  like a man with a bounty of over 4  billion berries i have 61 million  berries 100 for each subscriber ouch but  we're not trying to beat shanks we're  trying to beat a treble who has 99  million for the magical 100 million  berries in other words one million  subscribers and so not only can you help  me make this dream come true by  subscribing but you also get freshly  harvested one-piece content every single  week in return and so i think it would  truly make sense for the man who's  making sure to carry on raj's will as a  yonko to grab the most easily accessible  road poneglyph from fishman island and  put it on elbaf to protect it only for  the right person to see the man roger  was waiting for in other words luffy  shanks definitely knew about this road  poneglyph there because he traveled to  fishman island with roger albath is a  true fortress of an island just like one  all filled with some of the most  fearsome and powerful warriors in the  entire world so really what better place  to have the final road poneglyph hidden  then the next location that the striats  are probably heading to a place where  luffy can finally meet changs a place  where he can earn the right to the last  redstone and prove his worth as a yonko  and also a place where finally shanks  and blackbeard might face each other  once again as blackbeard would surely  come for that very same poneglyph as  well and if you really want to know what  has been foreshadowed about elbaf and  how the arc might play out in the end  and why shanks has such strong ties to  nordic mythology you should really not  miss out on these two videos right here
 

